Here is the commit message:
HADOOP-12052 IPC client downgrades all exception types to
 IOE, breaks callers trying to use them. (Brahma Reddy Battula via stevel)

Here is the root cause:
The bug occurred because the IPC client was downgrading all exceptions caught during the execution of remote calls to a generic `IOException`, preventing callers from recognizing specific exception types that may provide more meaningful context about the error. This behavior broke the expected contract for exception handling within the IPC framework, as callers relied on specific exceptions to implement appropriate error handling logic.

Here is the patch:
    * pool.  Connections to a given ConnectionId are reused. */
   private Connection getConnection(
       final ConnectionId remoteId,
       Call call, final int serviceClass, AtomicBoolean fallbackToSimpleAuth)
       throws IOException {
     if (!running.get()) {
       // the client is stopped
       throw new IOException("The client is stopped");
     }
     Connection connection;
     /* we could avoid this allocation for each RPC by having a  
      * connectionsId object and with set() method. We need to manage the
      * refs for keys in HashMap properly. For now its ok.
      */
     while(true) {
       try {
         connection = connections.get(remoteId, new Callable<Connection>() {
           @Override
           public Connection call() throws Exception {
             return new Connection(remoteId, serviceClass);
           }
         });
       } catch (ExecutionException e) {
-        throw new IOException(e);
+        Throwable cause = e.getCause();
+        // the underlying exception should normally be IOException
+        if (cause instanceof IOException) {
+          throw (IOException) cause;
+        } else {
+          throw new IOException(cause);
+        }
       }
       if (connection.addCall(call)) {
         break;
       } else {
         connections.invalidate(remoteId);
       }
     }

     //we don't invoke the method below inside "synchronized (connections)"
     //block above. The reason for that is if the server happens to be slow,
     //it will take longer to establish a connection and that will slow the
     //entire system down.
     connection.setupIOstreams(fallbackToSimpleAuth);
     return connection;
   }



