Reason:
The patch introduces logic to check the cause of the `ExecutionException`. If the cause is an `IOException`, it throws it directly, preserving the specific exception type. Otherwise, it wraps the cause in a new `IOException`. This change allows callers to receive the original exception type when possible, restoring the intended behavior of the IPC framework's exception handling.

